---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { buttonVariants } from '../../components/ui/Button';
---

<Layout title="Welcome to One Reader" description="A short guide to starting your first One Reader correspondence.">
  <header class="border-b border-border">
    <div class="shell flex min-h-20 items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <a class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] tracking-[-0.025em] no-underline" href="/" aria-label="One Reader, home">One Reader</a>
      <a class="text-sm text-muted-foreground underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground hover:underline" href="/member/">Your account</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content" class="shell py-16 sm:py-24 lg:py-32">
    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-border pb-16 md:grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.22fr] md:gap-20 md:pb-24">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-6">Welcome to One Reader</p>
        <h1 class="display balance">A small note before you begin.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="self-end">
        <p class="text-xl leading-9 text-muted-foreground">Thank you for joining One Reader. Your email is confirmed and your account is ready. One Reader is a service for writing to one person you do not know, without turning the exchange into a public performance.</p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">There is one practical thing to do now: open your account and tell us which languages you can write and read. That information is what lets us look for a thoughtful match.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-border py-16 md:grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.22fr] md:gap-20 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="start-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Start here</p>
        <h2 id="start-heading" class="section-title balance">Set up the room before you enter it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">In your account, add the languages in which you are comfortable writing and reading, choose whether you are available to receive letters, and complete the few details needed to keep age groups separate.</p>
        <a class={buttonVariants({ size: 'large' }) + ' mt-8'} href="/member/">Open your account</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-border py-16 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-20 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="service-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-5">How the service works</p>
        <h2 id="service-heading" class="section-title balance">One opening is free. The room is not a feed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        <p class="m-0">You can send one first letter for free. We find a reader who can understand your language, deliver the letter by email, and keep both addresses private. You can always receive letters and reply to conversations that are already open.</p>
        <p class="mt-6">If you want to write to someone new again, annual membership gives you one new opening every 24 hours. Its current price is shown in your local currency when you choose it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-border py-16 md:grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.22fr] md:gap-20 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="membership-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Why there is a membership</p>
        <h2 id="membership-heading" class="section-title balance">A contribution to a careful service.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        <p class="m-0">One Reader has no public profile to browse, no advertising feed, and no reason to make you spend more time here than the letter requires. The membership pays for the work of keeping the service private, moderated and deliberately small.</p>
        <p class="mt-6">It also sets a useful expectation. Someone who pays to open a new correspondence is making a clearer commitment to the exchange and to the person on the other side. It is not a guarantee that every letter will be perfect; it is a way of making the room a little more intentional.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 py-16 md:grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.22fr] md:gap-20 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="advice-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-5">A few ways to be here</p>
        <h2 id="advice-heading" class="section-title balance">Write to a person, and leave room for what writing can do.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="grid gap-4 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          <li>Come without a performance in mind. A stranger does not need a polished version of you.</li>
          <li>Be curious without being invasive. Protect private information and let the other person set their boundaries.</li>
          <li>Sometimes being read without judgment is already a meaningful thing. You do not have to fix, advise or impress.</li>
          <li>A reply is an invitation, not an obligation. You can continue, pause or leave room for silence.</li>
          <li>If something feels wrong, use the private report link in the email. We will review it carefully.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5">
          <a class={buttonVariants({ size: 'large' })} href="/member/">Set up my languages</a>
          <a class="text-sm text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground" href="/terms">Read the full terms</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    import { supabase } from '../../lib/supabase';

    const intentKey = 'dear-someone:signup-intent';
    const sessionResult = supabase ? await supabase.auth.getSession() : { data: { session: null } };
    const session = sessionResult.data.session;
    if (!session) {
      window.location.assign('/sign-in/');
    } else {
      const rawIntent = window.localStorage.getItem(intentKey);
      if (supabase) {
        try {
          const metadata = session.user.user_metadata ?? {};
          const intent = rawIntent
            ? JSON.parse(rawIntent)
            : metadata.plan_intent === 'free'
              ? {
                  source: 'signup',
                  plan: 'free',
                  countryCode: (navigator.language.split('-')[1] || '').toUpperCase() || null,
                  languageCode: navigator.language || 'en',
                  journalOptIn: metadata.journal_opt_in === true,
                  termsAccepted: metadata.terms_accepted === true,
                  privacyAcknowledged: metadata.privacy_acknowledged === true,
                }
              : null;
          if (intent) {
            const { error } = await supabase.functions.invoke('complete-signup', {
              body: intent,
              headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${session.access_token}` },
            });
            if (!error) window.localStorage.removeItem(intentKey);
          }
        } catch {
          // The account can still be completed from the account page.
        }
      }
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
